{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act criminal record screening limits","requirement":"A housing provider may not ask about or consider an applicant's criminal record before making a conditional offer, may after an offer consider only specified convictions after an individualized assessment, and may not advertise blanket exclusion of applicants with records.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent for residential purposes, excluding dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excludes dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."},"exemptions":"Dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"Director may impose up to $1,000 (no prior violation in five years), $5,000 (one prior), or $10,000 (two or more priors in seven years), and order cease and desist, compliance reporting, or a fee refund.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-55","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not require an applicant to complete any housing application that includes any inquiries regarding an applicant’s criminal record prior to the provision of a conditional offer","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act application fee disclosure and refund","requirement":"Before accepting any application fee, a housing provider must disclose in writing whether it reviews criminal history and that the applicant may submit evidence of inaccuracies, rehabilitation or other mitigating factors; the director may order the fee refunded.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent for residential purposes, excluding dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excludes dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."},"exemptions":"Dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"Director may require that the applicant's rental application fee be returned.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-55","quoted_span":"Prior to accepting any application fee, a housing provider shall disclose in writing to the applicant: (1) Whether the eligibility criteria of the housing provider include the review and consideration of criminal history; and","interaction":null,"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act eviction after overturned director order","requirement":"If a housing provider's successful appeal overturns the director's order to house an applicant, that reversal is grounds to evict the former applicant, so long as the provider gives at least 45 days' notice before the eviction.","key_value":"45 days' notice","coverage_conditions":"Former applicants housed in a rental dwelling unit as the result of a director's order later overturned on the housing provider's successful appeal.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Applies to renters housed under a director's order overturned on the housing provider's successful appeal."},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-63","quoted_span":"shall be grounds for the housing provider to evict the former applicant if that person resides in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director’s order, so long as the housing provider provides the applicant with at least 45 days’ notice prior to the eviction","interaction":"Notwithstanding the Anti-Eviction Act, P.L.1974, c.49 (C.2A:18-61.1 et seq.) to the contrary.","confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
